 "moshi_text": "Hello, how is it going? I think fruit and vegetable are two different types of food. So, fruit is the part of a plant that develops from the ovary after flowering and contains seeds. And vegetables are the edible parts of plants, like leaves, roots, and stems. So, fruit and vegetable are both part of the same plant, but they're different in terms of their structure and function. So, fruit is usually sweeter and has a higher sugar content, while vegetables are often bitter and have more vitamins and minerals. Starfruit is a tropical fruit that is native to Asia. It has a unique shape, with a bright green skin and a white, fleshy flesh inside. Watermelon is a sweet, refreshing fruit that is native to Africa. It is known for its juicy, watery flesh and its distinctive green rind. Dragonfruit is a tropical fruit that is native to Southeast Asia. It has a unique, spiky skin and a sweet, juicy flesh inside. Nectarine is a type of peach with a smooth, red skin. It is a hybrid of peach and cherry that is native to China. Breadfruit is a tropical fruit that is native to Southeast Asia. It has a large, edible seed that is often compared to bread in texture.",
